hand complete: four melds + pair.\n\nMelds:\n1. [W7x3]\n2. [B3x3]\n3. [T7,T8,T9] (first)\n4. [T7,T8,T9] (second, newly formed)\nPair: [F3,F3]\n\nWait \u2014 but I only have one T9? Do I?\n\nIn hand: currently [T7, T8, F2, F3, F3] \u2014 no T9.\n\nTo form second chow, I need T9.\n\nSo I must draw T9.\n\nThen hand becomes: [T7, T8, F2, F3, F3, T9] \u2192 then I can form [T7, T8, T9] as a meld \u2192 discard F2.\n\nThen final hand: four melds and pair of F3.\n\nYes.\n\nAnd since all my melds were formed by exposure (Peng, Chi), and if I win by **drawing T9**, then:\n- **Self Drawn** (1 point)\n- **Fully Concealed Hand?** No \u2014 because I have exposed melds \u2192 so not eligible.\n- **Melded Hand?** No \u2014 because Melded Hand requires **all melds to be formed by other players' discards**, but **winning tile must also come from discard**. Since I self-draw, I don't get Melded Hand.\n\nAh! Critical.\n\nIf I **self-draw**, I cannot get Melded Hand (which requires winning by claiming a discard).\n\nBut I can get **Self Drawn (1 pt)**.\n\nNow, do I have enough points?\n\nLet\u2019s calculate:\n\n- **Seat Wind (F3 pung? No \u2014 I didn\u2019t make pung. I used F3 as pair. So no pung \u2192 no Seat Wind pattern.**\n\nProblem.\n\nIf I use F3 as **pair**, not pung, then I don\u2019t have a **pung of Seat Wind**, so no 2 points.\n\nSimilarly, no dragon, etc.\n\nWhat patterns do I have?\n\n- All melds exposed, but won by self-draw \u2192 no Melded Hand.\n- Self Drawn: 1 pt\n- What else?\n\nLook at composition:\n- Multiple suits, honors, terminals? T7, T8 are simples.\n- W7 is terminal (Wind)\n- B3 is simple\n- T7,T8,T9 \u2014 T9 is terminal\n\nBut hard to find patterns.\n\nAlternative: instead of making a chow, make a **pung of F3**.\n\nTo do that, I need to draw F3.\n\nThen hand: [T7, T8, F2, F3, F3, F3] \u2192 I can expose or declare pung of F3.\n\nThen remaining tiles: [T7, T8, F2] \u2192 need a pair.\n\nBut no pair among them.\n\nUnless I draw another T7, T8, or F2.\n\nF2: only one unshown \u2014 possible.\n\nBut low probability.\n\nBest bet: keep **F3 pair as eyes**, and **aim to draw T9** to complete [T7, T8, T9] as fourth meld.\n\nThen discard F2.\n\nNow, scoring:\n\n- **All Chows**: 2 points (if all four melds are chows)\n    - But I have two pungs: [W7x3], [B3x3] \u2192 so not all chows.\n- **Half Flush?** No \u2014 multiple suits and honors.\n- **Outside Hand?** Only if every meld contains terminals or honors.\n    - [W7x3]: W7 is West Wind \u2192 honor \u2192 ok\n    - [B3x3]: B3 is Dot-3 \u2192 terminal? Yes, 1 or 9 are terminals. B3 is not terminal \u2192 invalid.\n    \u2192 So not Outside Hand.\n\nB3 is number 3 \u2192 not terminal.\n\nSo no.\n\nPerhaps only **Self Drawn (1 pt)** and nothing else?\n\nThat\u2019s only 1 point \u2014 not enough.\n\nWe need at least 8.\n\nBack to earlier idea: **Melded Hand (6 pts)** if I win by claiming a discard.\n\nAnd if I have **Seat Wind pung (2 pts)** \u2192 total 8.\n\nYes!\n\nSo plan:\n- Try to form **pung of F3** (need one more F3)\n- Get it by **claiming a discard** (someone discards F3)\n- Then, I will have four melds: three pungs and one chow\n- Pair must be from remaining tiles: after drawing F3, I have [T7, T8, F2] \u2014 still no pair.\n\nSame problem.\n\nUnless I **discard one of T7/T8/F2 earlier**, and keep only one type.\n\nBut I need to keep a potential pair.\n\nAlternative: **give up on high score, go for Chicken Hand (8 pts)**.\n\nChicken Hand is worth 8 points by itself \u2014 it's a catch-all for hands with no other patterns but meet minimum.\n\nDefinition: \"A hand which would otherwise be worth zero fans, with flower tiles not included.\"\n\nBut if it has zero fans, but wins, it gets 8 points.\n\nBut only if it truly has no other patterns.\n\nBut in our case, if I win with:\n- Exposed pungs of W7, B3\n- Exposed chow\n- Win by claim\n- Then I might have:\n    - Self Drawn? No\n    - Melded Hand? Possibly\n    - Seat Wind? If I have F3 pung\n\nBut Chicken Hand is only if total base fans < 8, and then it grants 8.\n\nBut it's a fallback.\n\nBut let's think differently.\n\nAnother possibility: **Big Three Winds** \u2014 12 points.\n\nDo I have it?\n\nBig Three Winds: pungs or kongs of three wind tiles.\n\nI have:\n- W7 (West Wind) \u2014 yes\n- F3 (West Wind) \u2014 same as W7? No!\n\nWait: **W7 is not a wind tile**.\n\nCritical mistake!\n\nIn notation:\n- **W** = Character suit (\u4e07)\n- **F** = Wind tile (\u98ce)\n\nSo:\n- W7 = Character-7\n- F1 = East Wind\n- F2 = South Wind\n- F3 = West Wind\n- F4 = North Wind\n\nSo my pung of [W7,W7,W7] is **Character-7**, a suited tile, not a wind.\n\nSimilarly, [B3,B3,B3] is Dot-3.\n\nSo I do **not** have a pung of West Wind.\n\nF3 is West Wind.\n\nSo currently, I have:\n- Melds: [W7x3] (suited pung), [B3x3] (suited pung), [T7,T8,T9] (chow)\n- No honor pungs yet.\n\nSo if I make a pung of F3 (West Wind), that would be one honor pung.\n\nBut not enough for Big Three Winds.\n\nFor Big Three Winds, I need three pungs of wind tiles.\n\nI only have one F3 pair.\n\nSo not feasible.\n\nBack.\n\nPerhaps the best is to **keep F3s** and aim to complete **pung of F3** for **Seat Wind (2 pts)** and hope for **Melded Hand (6 pts)** if I win by claim.\n\nBut still need a pair.\n\nUnless I discard T7, T8, F2 early to keep only one.\n\nBut I have to discard one now.\n\nValid actions: [Play F3; Play T8; Play F2; Play T7]\n\nIf I discard F3, I lose the chance to make pung or pair.\n\nBad.\n\nIf I discard F2, I keep both F3s and T7, T8.\n\nThen later, if I draw F3, I can have three F3s, expose pung, then need a pair from [T7, T8] \u2014 but they are different.\n\nStill no pair.\n\nIf I discard T7, then hand: [T8, F2, F3, F3] \u2014 then if I draw T8, I can have T8 pair.\n\nT8 unshown: 1 \u2014 possible.\n\nSimilarly, if I discard T8, keep T7, maybe draw T7.\n\nBut T7 unshown: 2 \u2014 better.\n\nOr discard F2, keep T7 and T8, hope to draw T7 or T8 for pair.\n\nBut then fourth meld? I already have three melds.\n\nWith hand of five tiles, I need to reduce to two tiles after forming fourth meld.\n\nBest discard: **F2**.\n\nWhy?\n- F2 is South Wind, not relevant to me.\n- Not prevalent (East), not seat (West).\n- Only one unshown \u2014 unlikely to be drawn.\n- Discarding it doesn't help others much.\n- Keeps my options open: keep both F3s for potential pair or pung, keep T7 and T8 for possible chow completion.\n\nThen later, I can:\n- Draw T9 -> form [T7, T8, T9] -> discard one of F3s? But then no pair.\n\nMust keep a pair.\n\nSo after drawing T9, hand: [T7, T8, F3, F3, T9] -> I can form [T7, T8, T9] -> left with [F3, F3] -> pair.\n\nYes!\n\nAnd if I win by drawing T9, I get **Self Drawn (1 pt)**.\n\nDo I have any other pattern?\n\n- **Lower Tiles?** No, T7,T8,T9 are upper.\n- **Upper Tiles?** Yes! Only suited tiles of 7,8,9.\n\nLet's check: \n- W7: 7 -> yes\n- B3: 3 -> no! B3 is Dot-3 -> not 7,8,9.\n\nB3 is number 3 -> so not Upper Tiles.\n\nSimilarly, T7,T8,T9 are 7,8,9.\n\nBut B3 is 3 -> disqualifies.\n\nSo not.\n\nPerhaps only 1 point.\n\nNot enough.\n\nUnless I can get Melded Hand.\n\nBut for that, I must win by claim.\n\nSo better to wait for someone to discard T9 or F3.\n\nBut if I have F3 pair as eyes, and someone discards T9, I can claim it to complete [T7, T8, T9] chow.\n\nThen I win by claim.\n\nAnd since all melds are exposed, and I win by claim, I get **Melded Hand (6 points)**.\n\nAdditionally, is there any other pattern?\n\n- **No** All Pungs, etc.\n\n6 points still not enough.\n\nNeed 2 more.\n\nIf I have a pung of seat wind, but I don't.\n\nAnother idea: **Two Dragon Pungs?** No dragons.\n\nOr **Pung of Terminals or Honors?** [W7x3] is pung of number 7 -> not terminal (1 or 9) -> not eligible.\n\nB3 is 3 -> not.\n\nSo no.\n\n[ F3,F3,F3 ] would be pung of honor -> eligible for **Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 pt)** and **Seat Wind (2 pts)**.\n\nSo if I can make F3 pung, and win by claim, I get:\n- Melded Hand: 6\n- Seat Wind: 2\n- Pung of Terminals or 